<title>USA: Fedex and UPS main cargo carriers at Newark.</title>
<headline>Fedex and UPS main cargo carriers at Newark.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Port Authority of New York and New Jersey said Federal Express and the United Parcel Service handled more cargo imported and exported at New Jersey's Newark airport than all other carrioers there during the first nine months of last year.</p>
<p>The top ten handlers of cargo of combined import and export tonnage handled at Newark in Jan-Sept 1996 were:</p>
<p>1.  Federal Express</p>
<p>2.  United Parcel Service</p>
<p>3.  Continental Airways</p>
<p>4.  Air Borne</p>
<p>5.  United Air Lines</p>
<p>6.  Scandinavian Airlines System</p>
<p>7.  American International Airlines</p>
<p>8.  Emery Worldwide</p>
<p>9.  Mountain Air</p>
<p>10. American Air Lines</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
